-- NOTE: `prisma migrate diff` also proposes rebuilding "CollaborativeUpdate"
-- to swap its primary key from `INTEGER NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT`
-- (created by 20260926000000_collaborative_update) to `"id" BIGINT NOT NULL
-- PRIMARY KEY`. That proposal is DELIBERATELY REJECTED: in SQLite only an
-- `INTEGER PRIMARY KEY` is a rowid alias and AUTOINCREMENT is valid only on
-- one, so Prisma 7 (which emits bare `BIGINT` with no autoincrement for a
-- SQLite `BigInt @id @default(autoincrement())`) produces a table where every
-- id-less insert fails its NOT NULL constraint. That silently breaks the collab
-- relay and the cross-replica rate-limit ledger — both of which fail open, so
-- the failure is invisible. Postgres is unaffected (BigInt maps to BIGSERIAL).
-- Leave the existing table untouched.

